<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Horn and East Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Dawro</h1><p class="st-meta">1500 CE – 1891 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">An Omotic kingdom of south-western Ethiopia, known for the great defensive stone wall attributed to its kings.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Dawro, also called Kullo, lay west of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-wolaita">Wolaita</a> between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/omo-river">Omo</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gojeb-river">Gojeb</a> rivers. Its royal dynasty is known from oral tradition, which places its consolidation in the 16th century, after the earlier Christian presence in the region had faded. The kingdom was closely related in language and culture to its neighbours Wolaita and Konta.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The kawo (king) ruled with regional officials and clan leaders. Dawro is best known for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/halala-kella">Halala Kella</a>, a stone wall running for well over 100 kilometres, attributed in tradition to King Halala and built to defend the realm. Its people farmed ensete and grain and traded with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-kaffa">Kaffa</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gibe-river">Gibe</a> kingdoms.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1891 Dawro was conquered by the armies of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/menelik-ii">Menelik II</a> and annexed to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/ethiopian-empire">Ethiopian Empire</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dawro-zone">Dawro Zone</a> today keeps the name, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/halala-kella">Halala Kella</a> wall is a significant heritage site.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1500 CE – 1891 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom